    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's more than just a concept for a poem though. i'm starting to think that maybe the only way to actually achieve that kind of raw honesty is to actually live it. like, if art is supposed to be the ultimate truth, then maybe the ultimate truth is just... the act of returning to nothing. creating something that is its own conclusion. do you think a person can actually find peace in that kind of finality?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
